WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.500
Welcome to our training on getting recommendations for new and existing case packs.

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:12.280
At Amazon, we support three package configuration types, Single Unit, Case Pack, and Pallet.

00:00:12.280 --> 00:00:17.990
In this video, we'll focus on case packs, which are common in higher-volume business-to-business

00:00:17.990 --> 00:00:22.020
or B2B sales and can help attract Amazon business customers.

00:00:22.660 --> 00:00:28.580
We'll demonstrate how sellers can use the Case Pack product opportunities tool to get recommendations.

00:00:28.940 --> 00:00:34.720
To use the Case Pack product opportunities tool, you need to meet two basic requirements.

00:00:35.180 --> 00:00:41.708
Be a professional seller and be either internal to a brand enrolled in Amazon Brand Registry or

00:00:41.708 --> 00:00:42.860
an authorized reseller.

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:46.920
To access the tool in Seller Central, open the main menu.

00:00:47.420 --> 00:00:50.900
Hover over B2B, then click B2B Central.

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:54.720
On the next page, click Case Pack Recommendations.

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:57.660
You'll see tabs for two kinds of recommendations.

00:00:57.880 --> 00:01:03.320
The first section, Add New Case Packs, shows products you currently sell as single units.

00:01:04.020 --> 00:01:09.440
These products aren't yet listed in the Amazon Store as case packs by you or other sellers.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:16.180
They belong to a brand enrolled in Brand Registry that you're either internal to or authorized by.

00:01:16.660 --> 00:01:22.976
The products in the Add New Case Packs section of the tool are ranked according to the number of

00:01:22.976 --> 00:01:26.300
orders you've received from Amazon business customers for multiple units.

00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:32.537
Multi-unit orders can be an indication that there may be demand for a product to be sold as a case

00:01:32.537 --> 00:01:32.800
pack.

00:01:32.800 --> 00:01:39.296
Next to each product, we list the number of orders you've received for five or more units in the

00:01:39.296 --> 00:01:39.980
last year.

00:01:39.980 --> 00:01:46.320
We also list the sales associated with those orders and provide a suggested size for a case pack.

00:01:46.320 --> 00:01:53.104
We base suggested case pack sizes on the number of units that Amazon business customers have most

00:01:53.104 --> 00:01:54.700
frequently purchased from you.

00:01:54.700 --> 00:02:01.040
If you decide to create a new case pack listing based on a recommendation, you have two options.

00:02:01.040 --> 00:02:06.800
You can click the Create Case Pack button to create a standalone listing for your case pack,

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:13.682
or you can click Enroll in Amazon Bulk Services to establish a package hierarchy and create a consolidated

00:02:13.682 --> 00:02:18.880
listing that features both your case pack and the product as a single unit.

00:02:18.880 --> 00:02:25.180
We recommend the second option because creating a consolidated listing makes it easier for customers

00:02:25.180 --> 00:02:29.800
to find, compare and purchase products in different quantities and configurations.

00:02:30.740 --> 00:02:37.740
Consolidated listings also automatically enroll case packs in Amazon Bulk Services or ABS.

00:02:37.740 --> 00:02:44.597
This program supports bulk B2B sales with enhanced tools and benefits, including lower referral

00:02:44.597 --> 00:02:46.740
fees on eligible case packs.

00:02:46.740 --> 00:02:53.490
If you decide to create a consolidated listing, click Enroll in Amazon Bulk Services to go to our

00:02:53.490 --> 00:02:55.740
Creating a Package Hierarchy Help page.

00:02:55.740 --> 00:03:01.157
This page provides step-by-step instructions for generating and completing an inventory file for

00:03:01.157 --> 00:03:07.657
both your case pack and the package hierarchy you want to establish between it and the single unit

00:03:07.657 --> 00:03:08.740
of the product.

00:03:08.740 --> 00:03:15.328
It also explains how to upload your inventory file to Seller Central to create your consolidated

00:03:15.328 --> 00:03:15.740
listing.

00:03:15.740 --> 00:03:22.666
In addition to reviewing the Help page, we encourage you to watch our Seller University video, Amazon

00:03:22.666 --> 00:03:26.740
Bulk Services create consolidated listings for case packs and Pallets.

00:03:26.740 --> 00:03:33.001
If you decide to create a standalone listing for your case pack instead of a consolidated one, click

00:03:33.001 --> 00:03:34.740
the Create Case Pack button.

00:03:34.740 --> 00:03:41.001
You'll be brought to product information pages where you can make entries and selections for your

00:03:41.001 --> 00:03:43.740
case pack using our standard listing process.

00:03:43.740 --> 00:03:49.666
The second section in the Case Pack Product Opportunities tool, Add New Offers, shows case packs

00:03:49.666 --> 00:03:53.740
that are already listed in the Amazon store by other sellers.

00:03:53.740 --> 00:04:00.036
Like the individual products on the previous tab, these case packs belong to a brand enrolled in

00:04:00.036 --> 00:04:03.740
brand registry that you're either internal to or authorized by.

00:04:03.740 --> 00:04:09.971
The case packs in the list are ranked according to the number of total orders that Amazon business

00:04:09.971 --> 00:04:12.740
customers placed for them in the last year.

00:04:12.740 --> 00:04:16.740
Next to each case pack, we provide a suggested price.

00:04:16.740 --> 00:04:22.740
We base suggested prices on current B2B featured offer prices for case packs.

00:04:22.740 --> 00:04:28.407
If you don't see a suggested price, that means there's currently no featured offer for the case

00:04:28.407 --> 00:04:28.740
pack.

00:04:28.740 --> 00:04:35.240
If you decide to match an offer to an existing case pack listing, click the Add an Offer button

00:04:35.240 --> 00:04:41.398
to go to the offer page where you can enter your pricing and quantity information using our standard

00:04:41.398 --> 00:04:41.740
process.

00:04:41.740 --> 00:04:48.169
Or if you want to add an offer and also create a consolidated listing for the case pack with its

00:04:48.169 --> 00:04:50.740
single unit or another configuration of the product,

00:04:50.740 --> 00:04:58.454
you can click Enroll in Amazon Bulk Services to go to the Amazon Bulk Services creating a package

00:04:58.454 --> 00:04:59.740
hierarchy help page.

00:04:59.740 --> 00:05:06.001
You'll use the same process we outlined earlier in this video, but will only need to provide offer

00:05:06.001 --> 00:05:07.740
information for the case pack.

00:05:07.740 --> 00:05:13.340
In addition to viewing recommendations within the Case Pack Product Opportunities tool, you can

00:05:13.340 --> 00:05:17.740
use the Download Report button to save recommendations in a spreadsheet.

00:05:17.740 --> 00:05:23.740
This can help create a record of the recommendations we provide, which are refreshed regularly.

00:05:23.740 --> 00:05:29.772
Remember that while using any part of the Case Pack Product Opportunities tool, the tool might not

00:05:29.772 --> 00:05:34.740
include every product or case pack you can create or match a listing for.

00:05:34.740 --> 00:05:40.740
This concludes our training on getting recommendations for new and existing case packs.

00:05:40.740 --> 00:05:43.740
Thank you and happy selling in the Amazon store!
